#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""email-gatekeeper -- one access point for a firm's mail, and nothing else.

WHAT THIS IS. Humans and agents talk across organisations. One address per
organisation rather than one per person, with a service behind it that routes
what arrives to the sessions it concerns and carries what they write back out.
The service is the plumbing. Every judgement about a mail lives somewhere else.

THE LAW THIS SERVICE RUNS UNDER.

  1. IT NEVER READS A MAIL FOR MEANING. It applies a table. The one line it puts
     on the bus is the provider's own preview field, truncated, never composed.
     Nothing here calls a model, and nothing here ever should.
  2. IT NEVER DECIDES A RECIPIENT beyond applying that table, and it never
     replies on its own. A mail is information and it grants nothing.
  3. NO SECRET ON DISK. The provider key is resolved once at start, from a
     reference, through the machine credential systemd hands this unit. It is
     held in memory and passed to an adapter in that adapter's environment. It
     is never written, never logged, and never put on a command line.
  4. NO CORRESPONDENCE HERE. Mail rests at the provider. This service keeps a
     routing table, a thread map, a send log and the position a catch-up
     starts from. Message text is fetched on demand and is not stored.
  5. IT NEVER REFUSES A CALLER. Anybody who can open the socket can send. The
     runbook is the rule and the log is the audit. What that costs is written in
     the email skill's reference/mail-service.md rather than hidden here.

WHAT IS CORE AND WHAT IS AN ADAPTER. This file knows about mail, handles, a
routing table and a socket. It knows nothing about how mail is fetched or sent.
That is an adapter, because the provider is exactly the thing that differs per
firm and per year. This is master-builder's Adapters primitive
(skill-primitives.md), and it is the same shape the wake rail uses.

THE WAKE IS NOT THIS SERVICE'S JOB. A bus message is the whole act. `bus-nudge`
already sweeps every handle on every bus it watches and tells a live session it
has unread mail, once per newest message id, same account only. A second
delivery path here would carry its own consent story and its own way to fail
quietly, and it would reach nothing the standing rail does not.

  email-gatekeeper --check     resolve everything, probe the adapter, serve
                               nothing, connect to nothing
  email-gatekeeper --serve     the unit runs this

EXIT CODES. 0 ok. 2 usage. 3 nothing here can reach a provider, or the key could
not be resolved. Both are walls and both are loud.
"""

